  "literal_sha256": "fe84fc55cab4c323370a8f0bc02ef513d3ed3121819a5d76ab6a2717604b1ba0",
  "scope": "All 52 units of the complete declared constituent: 19 selected proper Canon blocks on printed176,177,181,183,184; dedicated CANON MISSÆ title and complete facing Crucifixion context; body title and every included prayer, rubric, internal heading, placeholder, inline cross, spoken cue and final chant word on printed203–213. Ends with final Per omnia/Amen and adjacent Iungit manus, before Orémus. Every one of the 18 selected source pages was directly viewed. This receipt does not claim whole-Missal completeness or an independent search for additional forms outside the declared selection.",
  "method": "One distinct reviewer directly inspected all 18 original-derived full-page PNGs, with enlarged source crops where accents, abbreviation marks, printed spellings or punctuation needed resolution. The five-page tail and eight-page title/opening sequence were read independently before their draft batches were opened; the five prefatory proper-form pages were read from images before proper-forms.json was opened. All 19 proper blocks, all main Canon bodies and their source joins, all 25 inline crosses, seven N. placeholders and the final response cue were compared to the exact final candidate-v5 bodies. Ten tail loci, two opening loci and six proper-form loci were reconciled against original-size images. All six proper corrections and both opening corrections were rechecked in the final frozen bodies; the tail corrections and physical joins were also confirmed. Binding, extent, literal artifact and all 52 unit hashes were recomputed; every body equals its exact selected normalized bytes; census-to-unit page incidence was checked in both directions. All 18 embedded PDF JPEGs were extracted and matched byte-for-byte to the extent original_image_sequence hashes. The reviewed native DjVu deliveries match every original source hash in that sequence. Original images, not OCR, familiar Roman wording or another edition, control acceptance.",
  "normalization_limit": "NFC UTF-8; long s becomes s; unambiguous printed abbreviation signs expand as listed in the source-block audit; physical wraps and line-end division hyphens disappear. Source u/v, i/j, æ/œ, accents, case including display initials, punctuation, &c., alternatives, every included rubric and spoken cue remain. Pattée crosses are represented by ✠ and the response cue by ℟.; word-separating spaces are regularized. Each stored line is one consecutive source block or paragraph, with source page/column/baseline and ink classes retained separately. No heading, quotation wrapper, modern translation, or explanatory material is inserted into literal text. Proper forms retain their discontiguous prefatory locations and are not relocated into the main Canon. Type colour, spatial geometry and music pitches are retained in the facsimile and source maps rather than asserted as a musical or glyph-diplomatic transcription. The isolated red cross above the body title is treated as title ornament; the 25 inline ceremonial crosses remain in text.",
  "findings_resolved": [
    "209 left 1: VNde → VNdè; distinct grave on final e.",
    "210 right 16: San ✠ guinem → Sán ✠ guinem; explicit acute on a.",
    "211 left 3 and right 12–13: eúndem → eúmdem; both occurrences print m.",
    "211 left 8: MÉmento → MÉménto; capital É and following lowercase é both accented.",
    "211 left 14: fidei → fídei; source acute on i.",
    "211 left 18: aliquántulum → aliquantulùm; a expansion bar supplies n, while final u bears grave.",
    "211 left 19: defúnctis → defunctis; nasal expansion bar is not an acute.",
    "211 right 6: quiescéntibus → quiescentibus; e expansion bar is not an acute.",
    "212 left 10: Martýribus → Martyribus; no acute over y.",
    "203 left 16: vt accépta → vti accépta; source i and dot are distinct.",
    "208 right 15: secretè: → secretò:; final letter is o with grave.",
    "176 left, first Maríæ in Nativity proper: Máriæ → Maríæ; source acute is on i. The second wrapped Ma-/ríæ was already correct.",
    "177 right, Epiphany proper: Máriæ → Maríæ; source acute on i.",
    "181 right, Easter proper: Máriæ → Maríæ; source acute on i.",
    "183 left, Ascension proper: Máriæ → Maríæ; source acute on i.",
    "181 right, Easter Communicantes: secúndum → secúndùm; acute first u and grave final u.",
    "184 right, Pentecost Hanc: Spíritu sáncto → Spíritu sancto; no acute on a. Easter Hanc separately retains source sáncto and qúæsumus.",
    "Cross-column rubric spans corrected to 209 left17–19/right1 and 211 left16–20/right1–3; 213 bis signat inter rubric ends left15, not left16."
  ],
  "reading_decisions": [
    "204 left2 Re- remains unaccented. The pale shape above e is show-through-like and lacks the distinct dark stroke of the actual source acute accents nearby; no acute is supplied.",
    "213 final Amen retains its period. The lower stop is distinct; a pale upper shape was examined in both original PNG and corresponding JPEG and does not justify replacing the stop with a colon.",
    "Internal Commemoratio pro viuis, Infra actionem and Commemoratio pro Defunctis headings are included. Repeated running heads, foliation, catchwords and preface chants outside the selected proper blocks are excluded by the stated constituent boundary.",
    "Source oddities and unequal abbreviations remain, including Nativity móriam, Easter secúndùm and qúæsumus, main COmmunicantes without an added acute, Ioannis without an added acute in the second saint-list occurrence, eúmdem, and the printed dot after the first Quam cross.",
    "Per at the foot of205 joins eúmdem at206; san-/cti and pecca-/tóribus join across their physical boundaries; no familiar conclusion is supplied."
  ],
